NNAAMMEE
       dpkg-realpath - print the resolved pathname with DPKG_ROOT support

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       ddppkkgg--rreeaallppaatthh [_o_p_t_i_o_n...] _p_a_t_h_n_a_m_e

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       ddppkkgg--rreeaallppaatthh is a tool (since dpkg 1.20.1) to resolve a pathname, that
       takes the ddppkkgg(1) root directory into account, either implicitly from
       the DDPPKKGG__RROOOOTT environment variable or from the command-line ----rroooott or
       ----iinnssttddiirr options, and returns an absolute _p_a_t_h_n_a_m_e relative to the
       root directory.  The root directory must not be prefixed to the
       _p_a_t_h_n_a_m_e to be resolved.

       This is intended to be used by other ddppkkgg helpers, or by maintainer
       scripts instead of using rreeaallppaatthh(1) or rreeaaddlliinnkk(1) to canonicalize
       pathnames, as these latter commands do not support canonicalization
       relative to a different root than _/.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       --zz, ----zzeerroo
           Use a NUL byte to end output lines instead of a new line character
           (since dpkg 1.20.6).

       ----iinnssttddiirr _d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y
       ----rroooott _d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y
           Set the root directory to _d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y, which is the base directory
           that pathnames get canonicalized against.  Defaults to «//» if
           DDPPKKGG__RROOOOTT has not been set.

       --??, ----hheellpp
           Show the usage message and exit.

       ----vveerrssiioonn
           Show the version and exit.

